ist_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it.\npytest isn't installed, so I'll run the same assertions directly.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. I couldn't run the test suite because pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the same assertions directly with `python3`, and they all pass.\n\n**Why it was wrong:** `round(x, 2)` rounds the number as the computer stores it, and `2.675` is stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so it rounds down. `round()` also sends exact halves to the even digit (`0.125 \u2192 0.12`), which doesn't match the \"half up\" promise in the function's docstring.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now rounds the number as written (`\"2.675\"`) rather than as stored, always rounding halves up. That's `Decimal(repr(x)).quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), ROUND_HALF_UP)`. It still returns a float, so code that calls it, like `add_vat`, doesn't change.\n\n**Results from the direct run:**\n- `2.675 \u2192 2.68`, `1.005 \u2192 1.01`, `0.125 \u2192 0.13`, `2.674 \u2192 2.67`, `3 \u2192 3.0`\n- Negative halves round away from zero: `-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`.\n- `add_vat` on an amount that comes to 2.675 after VAT gives `2.68`.\n- The existing `split` test still passes.\n\nI also added these cases as a test file, `tests/test_round_money.py`, which will run once pytest is installed.\n\n**Not fixed:** `split()` builds cents with `int(total * 100)`, which cuts off instead of rounding. Some amounts would come out a cent short (e.g. `int(0.29 * 100) == 28`), and the leftover cent would then go to the first share. I left it alone because it's outside what you asked; say if you want it fixed too.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 212659, "requests_cache_write": 16533, "requests_cost_usd": 0.17316879999999998, 